south africa's governing party the  african national congress has been  plagued by internal divisions for years  a poorly performing economy a lack of  service delivery and allegations of  corruption have added to a decline in  support  this conference  has demonstrated more clearly  that  more than ever before  our common commitment to lead our  organization of  fictionalism  patronage and corruption  and to renew and  to rebuild our organization  is quite  an urgent mission  critics blame the party's leaders for  failing to address some of south  africa's challenges despite three  decades of democracy inequality is rife  and many poor communities still don't  have access to running water and  electricity president ramaphosa says  fraud and corruption are to blame but  his efforts to end the scourge have been  weakened by a corruption scandal  he's been accused of concealing the  theft of four million dollars from his  game farm there are massive global  forces that have to be taken into  account but mal administration poor  management of the economy particularly  in the state-owned enterprises  not doing what was actually indicated by  anc governments in the late 1990s around  securing the energy sector um having a  better education system at both basic  and tertiary level to ensure that people  are employable and to transform social  space as well as the economy so that  more people find ownership in it to  broaden the tax base none of these  things have been done the conference  aimed to come up with solutions to some  of the most urgent problems including  unemployment of 35 percent and rising  poverty but it's not expected the anc  will immediately resolve any of these  key challenges and instead will put  forward recommendations to be discussed  later familia miller al jazeera  johannesburg
 

